# The append-only streams (`data/log/*.jsonl`, `data/todos.jsonl`) used to be
# tracked and carried `merge=union`, so two machines appending different lines
# merged without ever raising a conflict. They are not tracked any more — the
# repo holds the app, not what you have done with it — so those rules would now
# apply to nothing, and are removed rather than left here to be believed.
#
# The *read-side* handling they relied on is still in place and still earns its
# keep, because duplicated and out-of-order lines can arrive from any direction
# and not only from a merge: events sort by `ts`, stably, so a `session, undo,
# session` inside one second keeps file order and resolves to *checked*, and the
# fold is last-wins throughout. `backend/tests/test_sync.py` still pins all of
# it, and should keep doing so.

